We want to find $G(y_1, y_2) = P(Y_1 \leq y_1, Y_2 \leq y_2)$ for $0 < y_1 < y_2 < \infty$.

The event $\{Y_1 \leq y_1, Y_2 \leq y_2\}$ is equivalent to $\{\min(X_1, X_2) \leq y_1, \max(X_1, X_2) \leq y_2\}$.
Since $Y_1 \leq Y_2$ always holds, the condition $Y_1 \leq y_1$ and $Y_2 \leq y_2$ implies that both $X_1$ and $X_2$ must be less than or equal to $y_2$.
Specifically, $\min(X_1, X_2) \leq y_1$ means at least one of them is $\leq y_1$.
$\max(X_1, X_2) \leq y_2$ means both of them are $\leq y_2$.
So the event is $\{X_1 \leq y_2, X_2 \leq y_2\} \cap \{X_1 \leq y_1 \text{ or } X_2 \leq y_1\}$.
Since $y_1 < y_2$, the condition $\{X_1 \leq y_2, X_2 \leq y_2\}$ is the larger set.
